# Rebuild: counting cards on the beat

Remake this format with the user's own clips, in any editor. Work through the steps in order. Times are frames at 30 fps: f30 is one second. A range from fA to fB ends just before fB.

## 1. Sequence
- 1080 x 1920 (9:16), 30 fps, 180 frames (6.000s)
- import every clip listed under "Your clips"
- a clip of another size or shape is scaled to fill the frame and the overflow cropped; no black bars

## 2. Picture
Fill each slot with footage that matches "fill with". Cut where the original cut so the rhythm stays. Never stretch or slow a clip to fill time; trim instead. Pick clips by looking at their thumbnails.

| slot | from | to | length | fill with | clips long enough |
|------|------|----|--------|-----------|-------------------|
| HOOK | f0 | f60 | 2.000s | the first item, held still and centred | pour.mp4 |
| BUILD | f60 | f120 | 2.000s | the second item, same framing | pour.mp4 |
| PAYOFF | f120 | f180 | 2.000s | the result, wider | pour.mp4 |

Shots inside the slots:

| shot | from | to | length | slot | camera |
|------|------|----|--------|------|--------|
| 1 | f0 | f60 | 2.000s | HOOK | unknown |
| 2 | f60 | f120 | 2.000s | BUILD | unknown |
| 3 | f120 | f180 | 2.000s | PAYOFF | unknown |

## 3. Captions
Make every caption editable text, not burned into the picture. Positions are the centre of the text as a fraction of the frame (0,0 top left) and in pixels.

- style C1: Arial Black, about 118 px, fill #FEFFFF, outline #000104, box none, all caps

Text: no script was given. Write each caption from what is said in the clip under it (transcripts under "Your clips", word times in rebuild/assets.json), about as long as the original line. Show the lines to the user before building.

| id | from | to | kind | style | text | original | centre | pixels | animation |
|----|------|----|------|-------|------|----------|--------|--------|-----------|
| c1 | f0 | f60 | caption | C1 | from the clip's speech | ONE | (0.50, 0.18) | (539, 342) | none |
| c2 | f60 | f120 | caption | C1 | from the clip's speech | TWO | (0.50, 0.50) | (538, 955) | none |

## 4. Transitions
Every shot change is a hard cut.

## 5. Sound
- clip audio: keep the speech of the clips you place
- music from f15 to f180, with a steady beat
  - clips with music in them: shelf.mp4
- [tick] at f14: found in pour.mp4 at f40

## 6. Look
flat primaries: solid colour cards, no grade

## 7. Rules
- Cut on the beat, every 2 seconds.
- One short uppercase word per caption, centred.
- The payoff has no caption.

## 8. Done when
- the sequence is 180 frames at 30 fps and 1080 x 1920
- the picture cuts at f60, f120 (each within 1 frame)
- every caption above shows at its frames, place and style, as editable text
- no frame is black or empty, and no clip is stretched
- the export plays start to end; watch it next to the original

